<title>RUSSIA: Irkutskenergo has H1 IAS loss.</title>
<headline>Irkutskenergo has H1 IAS loss.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1996-11-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months ended June 30</p>
<p>				    1996	   1995</p>
<p>    Sales ($ million)	   435.47	    n/a</p>
<p>    Gross margin	     72.16	    n/a</p>
<p>    Loss before tax	  13.70	    n/a</p>
<p>    Loss after tax	   18.48	    n/a</p>
<p>    Accounts receivable   330.37	 282.43</p>
<p>    Shareholders funds  4,813.31     4,834.78</p>
<p>NOTES - 1995 comparisons as of Dec 31 not June 30. Figures are not audited, but are prepared to international accounting standards (IAS) by KPMG. Full name Irkutskoye AO Energetiki i Elektrifikatsii  0#IRGZ.RUO.</p>
<p>Company has applied to U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission to issue level-one American Depositary Receipts.</p>
<p>Company is 40 percent state-owned, management and employees own 10 percent, and other Russian and foreign shareholders own 50 percent.</p>
<p>--Jonathan Lynn, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
